        question: "What's the difference between attached and ballasted solar mounting structurally?",
        answer: "Attached systems penetrate the roof and connect mechanically to the framing — the engineering verifies the connection capacity into the actual members, the added point loads on those members, and the waterproofing details at every penetration. Ballasted systems sit on the roof held by weight — the engineering verifies the roof can carry the ballast plus panels as added dead load and proves the wind design keeps the array stable without mechanical attachment. Ballasted avoids penetrations but adds more weight; attached adds less weight but lives or dies on connection quality. I see the most problems with attached systems on roofs where the framing layout was assumed rather than verified — the lag bolts have to hit structure, not hope.",
