    description: "EV charger installs often need a PE stamp for electrical load analysis, panel capacity, and structural review of canopy chargers, plus Title 24 in California.",
    h1: "Do EV Charger Installations Need a PE Stamp?",
    answer: "EV charger installations need a PE stamp whenever the AHJ requires engineered electrical or structural documents — which is increasingly the norm for commercial sites, multi-charger installations, and any project adding significant load to an existing service. The electrical review verifies the load analysis: the charger's demand added to the building's existing loads, the panel and feeder capacity to carry it, and the service's headroom. The structural review applies to canopy-mounted chargers and any installation adding equipment weight to structures. A single Level 2 charger on a house with panel space is usually a standard permit; a bank of DC fast chargers at a retail site is an engineered project.\n\nWhat I check electrically starts with the load calculation. EV chargers are continuous loads, and the code treats continuous loads with a sizing factor that surprises owners expecting a simple breaker addition. I verify the existing panel's bus rating and available capacity, the feeder sizes, and whether the service itself needs upsizing — because discovering at inspection that the 400-amp service can't carry the new charging bank is a project-killer. Utility coordination runs in parallel: many utilities require their own application for load additions of this size, with transformer and service upgrade timelines that dwarf the permit timeline.\n\nIn California, Title 24 adds a layer: the state's energy code has EV charging infrastructure requirements for new construction and major alterations that the electrical design must satisfy, and the compliance documentation is part of the sealed set. Canopy chargers add the structural scope — the canopy's columns, foundations, and the charger mounting all get engineered for gravity, wind, and seismic. When the loads verify, the service is adequate or the upgrade is designed, and the structural scope checks out, the PE seals.",
